WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.960
[Narrator:] South of Savannah, the waves of
the Atlantic break on the shores 

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.840
of the golden isles of Georgia. 

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:47.400
Once the rendezvous of buccaneers, later scene of rich manorial plantations,

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:52.180
these islands have character and charm.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:55.490
Witness the picturesque ruins of the old slave hospital

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:01.480
where Negro slaves were treated more than a century ago.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:10.600
Westward the marshes of Glynn and the Sidney
Lanier oak under which the poet sat while

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.090
he wrote the songs that have made these marshes
famous.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:21.080
On the main, its harbor sheltered by the sea
island is the old town of Brunswick,

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:26.840
county seat of Glynn County, rich in traditions, important port of the old south, 

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.979
thriving seafood and industrial center of the new.

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:38.979
Here are important crab and shrimp fisheries,
canneries to preserve the catch for shipment.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:47.629
One of the South's largest wood pulp mills,

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.800
a modern plant for distillation of pine oil and other wood by-products...

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.420
a thriving veneer and box industry, all together giving employment

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.380
to thousands of workmen.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:03.739
Brunswick, center of a rural area, is typical
of communities throughout America.

00:02:03.739 --> 00:02:06.799
Here a demonstration in syphilis control can be carried on, 

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:10.979
a test program for work at other places, south or north.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:15.400
The United States Public Health Service joined
with the health departments of Georgia and

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:21.090
Glynn County to set up such a project. This
is not the story of syphilis, the disease;

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:27.310
it is the story of public health organizations
who stamp out syphilis.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:32.319
In Brunswick, the work resembles that of any city. Private doctors are given free drugs

00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:36.959
to treat all their cases of syphilis, so that
those who can afford to pay but little

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:39.619
may go to their own doctors. 

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:46.400
Thus the private physician treats those who can't afford to pay at all.

00:02:53.209 --> 00:03:00.249
At the health department, a modern public
clinic treats 275 patients each week free of charge.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:05.360
Systematic efforts have been made
to find syphilis, bring it to treatment.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:11.740
Blood tests are a part of school health examination.
Every child here has already been tested.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:18.220
In small communities in the outlying region
the story is the same. 

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:23.880
Here at St. Simon's, 35 patients come to the clinic each week.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.840
And rural doctors receive free drugs and financial

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:35.900
aid for the treatment of poorer patients, just
as do the doctors of the town.

00:03:44.639 --> 00:03:51.189
Up beyond the towns, beyond the doctors' offices,
beyond even roads, are the woods.

00:03:51.189 --> 00:03:56.989
This is a rural land, a land of forests, fewer than ten people to the square mile, 

00:03:56.989 --> 00:04:02.249
deep in the piney woods. How would one reach these people?

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:08.500
How reach those who work at country saw mills,
who gather gum from the pine trees and tend

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:13.730
the turpentine stills? Here are people who
have neither means for travel to urban centers,

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.230
nor leisure to travel.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:20.790
The health officer must reach these too if
he is to meet his responsibility for the protection

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:27.790
of the community. If this mountain will not
come to Mohammed, Mohammed must go to the mountain.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:36.120
Hence, a mobile clinic that travels throughout
three counties, Camden, McIntosh and Glynn.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.750
Let's follow its journeys day by day.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.740
Monday 107 miles, 106 patients. 

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:55.240
Tuesday 110
miles, 129 patients. 

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.460
Wednesday 102 miles, 118 patients.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:05.140
Thursday 40 miles, 40 patients. 

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:09.440
Friday 100 miles, 90 patients. 

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.660
Saturday 60 miles, 44 patients.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:19.420
For the week: 519 miles, 527 patients
at 24 clinics.

00:05:28.069 --> 00:05:33.599
This silver top is the symbol of the service.
Along the road, the clinic itself becomes

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:40.599
a bus to bring patients who live at intermediate
points to the treatment center.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:53.990
The clinic stops, the patients gather.

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:10.320
Next to church, the biggest event of the week.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.660
Find syphilis, bring it to treatment,

00:06:13.669 --> 00:06:15.669
that is the story of control. 

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:23.580
The treatment renders the patient non-infectious, stops the spread of the disease through the community.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:37.879
It's a far cry from the swift and shining
trailer to the oxcart, but many come to the

00:06:37.879 --> 00:06:40.679
clinic in this way, while many more come on foot, 

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:49.000
some walking ten miles or more for treatment once a week for 70 weeks.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.760
They gather at that rural forum, the country
store, 

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:57.760
to compare notes on this new contribution to the life of the community.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:10.590
The school bus serves in a new capacity. It
brings more patients to the clinic.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:34.440
Doctors on wheels, the clinical methods of
the finest hospitals reach out to serve a rural life.

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:45.939
Inside the trailer is a completely equipped
clinic. Electric sterilizers, refrigerator,

00:07:45.939 --> 00:07:50.879
fans, and lights are fed by a 110-volt generator in the tow car. 

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.720
No time is wasted in setting up for work. 

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.900
Three minutes after arrival treatment can begin.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:10.319
The clinic serves as a health center not only
for syphilis. This boy is being immunized

00:08:10.319 --> 00:08:17.319
against typhoid fever. At crowded stops the
county nurse sets up her stand nearby.

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:23.200
In the forward part of the trailer, blood
is taken for laboratory tests. 

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.200
Arsphenamine is administered. 

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:28.680
Two patients may be treated
at once. 

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:37.720
Here a specimen of blood is taken for a test.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:54.520
Arsphenamine injected into the blood kills
the germ of syphilis,

00:08:54.620 --> 00:09:00.960
and the patient can no longer transmit the disease to others.

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:07.990
Each patient gets simply written detailed
instructions so that the illness will be fully understood.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:24.230
Behind the curtain in the rear of the trailer
is a complete examination room 

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:28.750
with its own equipment and sterilizer. Here bismuth is administered. 

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:35.940
Bismuth prevents the tragic relapses of heart and brain.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:44.080
At health department headquarters in Brunswick, darkfield examinations are performed. 

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:47.080
A little serum from the first sore is examined under
the microscope.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.440
This is the earliest  possible diagnosis for syphilis.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:56.740
The earlier treatment is begun, the surer
the cure.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:11.180
It would take thirty-five hundred of these
syphilis germs laid end to end to make an inch. 

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:16.980
Spirochaeta pallida, a killer at large.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:26.120
At Waycross, sixty miles from Brunswick, Georgia
has a modern branch laboratory.

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:30.300
Here blood tests are performed for the Tri-County project.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:32.870
Tubes filled with blood specimens come from
the trailer, 

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:39.080
from the Brunswick clinic, and from private physicians.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:43.440
An automatic pipette measures serum into test
tubes for the Kahn test. 

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.640
Trained laboratory technicians are essential.

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:51.280
Laboratories can't
afford to make mistakes. Let's see the result.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:11:00.960
Negative, no syphilis. Negative, no syphilis.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.520
Positive reaction. 

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:08.900
Note the heavy particles in the tube -- that means syphilis.

00:11:09.770 --> 00:11:14.350
But one must be very sure. Let us doublecheck with a Wassermann test. 

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:22.440
That is another blood test for syphilis, technically a little different from the Kahn. Let's see what it will show.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:26.070
A milky fluid like this in the tube on the
right would mean syphilis. 

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:29.700
The clear tube is a check tube and here are the tests.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:36.710
Watch the tube on the right: negative, no
syphilis. Negative, no syphilis.

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:41.940
Positive. Here our case of syphilis is verified. 

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:47.390
Even the layman can see the difference in these two tubes.

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:53.490
The project is organized for finding cases
and holding them in treatment. 

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:57.140
It takes 70 weeks to ensure a cure for syphilis. 

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:02.180
Even with free treatment, it is not always easy to keep patients coming week after week.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:09.920
The trailer helps, but there are four follow-
up workers, two white and two colored.

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:18.850
The house-to-house canvass has proved also a most effective means of getting blood specimen.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:35.510
Behind the project, too, is education. One
must carry this story to the people.

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:41.700
Midwives deliver 400 babies a year in these counties.
Well- trained by the health department,

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.140
they are licensed by the state.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:47.330
Here they learn about the blood tests and
actual demonstration. 

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:54.020
They carry forth the story and bring mothers in for prenatal blood tests.

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:59.780
The grocery man wraps up the clinic announcement
with every purchase.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:18.710
The country store shares a place among its
tobacco signs for clinic hand bills.

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:39.120
Wherever the workers go, they tell the story
of the clinic to willing ears.

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:49.640
How bad blood makes people sick, how it destroys
heart and brain, how it makes babies die,

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:58.840
how the blood test finds it, and how the treatment, if taken long enough, is certain cure.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:07.020
The blood test serves a double purpose. First, it is a dragnet for syphilis.

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:13.520
Second, it is an educational device. Blood specimens are taken in the turpentine woods,

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:18.880
at factory gates, on the shrimp wharves, at the docks
of the [inaudible] fisherman.

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:24.720
A man who has seen the blood test loses his fear. The man who hasn't had one wants it.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:31.730
Everyone talks about it; the blood test becomes
a demonstration and a symbol.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:43.950
Youth faces its problem more directly, honestly,
spontaneously then did its father.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:50.950
Here, the blood test carries its message to a country dance hall.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:13.160
But the greatest help comes from the churches,
Pastors are ever willing and glad to cooperate.

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:19.090
They urge their people to join in the program.

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:28.670
They tell them of a disease which threatens
health and life and the generation yet unborn.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:36.200
They urge that the message will be carried
forth to the countryside,

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:40.660
that all may know and walk in the light of health.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:51.970
They themselves take the blood test as a demonstration and urge their parishioners to follow them.

00:15:55.240 --> 00:16:00.580
Such is the story of a community mobilized,
a community which met syphilis with the weapons

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:06.800
of medicine and modern public health. Whatever
you may do in your community, in these three

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:12.040
counties of southeastern Georgia, the days
of syphilis are numbered.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:19.040
Syphilis will be the next great plague to
go.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:24.840
[Gospel choir sings Walking in the Light of God] 

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:30.380
[Image of the clinic bus traveling down the road...

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:53.040
and people walking through the woods and along paths and roads, 

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:58.680
or traveling in an ox-drawn cart.]

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:14.200
[Gospel singing continues, with images of people traveling toward town, and the clinic bus doing the same.]

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:43.080
[Eventually all gather at the mobile clinic in town, awaiting evaluations and treatment.]

00:17:54.840 --> 00:18:10.400
[Their work complete, the health care workers and the clinic bus drive away from town.]

